WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.550
Before we begin the technical material let

00:00:02.563 --> 00:00:04.340
us quickly review how to use this

00:00:04.353 --> 00:00:08.053
interactive lesson Each slide contains one main

00:00:08.079 --> 00:00:11.645
idea Some slides explain a concept and

00:00:11.671 --> 00:00:15.461
other slides contain executable Python code You

00:00:15.474 --> 00:00:17.105
can move through the lesson by using

00:00:17.132 --> 00:00:19.316
the Next and Previous buttons the arrow

00:00:19.342 --> 00:00:21.132
keys or the slide menu at the

00:00:21.158 --> 00:00:23.618
top of the page When you reach

00:00:23.632 --> 00:00:26.197
a code example first read the explanation

00:00:26.224 --> 00:00:28.974
above the editor Then look through the

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.750
code from top to bottom Try to

00:00:31.763 --> 00:00:33.553
predict what the code will do before

00:00:33.579 --> 00:00:35.961
you run it When you are ready

00:00:36.171 --> 00:00:39.250
click the Run button The result appears

00:00:39.276 --> 00:00:41.303
in the terminal area below the code

00:00:42.224 --> 00:00:44.368
Compare the terminal output with what you

00:00:44.382 --> 00:00:47.947
expected After that make a small change

00:00:48.855 --> 00:00:51.382
For example change one number one name

00:00:51.566 --> 00:00:54.355
or one input value Then run the

00:00:54.368 --> 00:00:56.079
cell again and see how the output

00:00:56.105 --> 00:00:59.342
changes Small experiments are one of the

00:00:59.368 --> 00:01:02.276
best ways to learn programming If you

00:01:02.289 --> 00:01:04.711
accidentally change the code too much you

00:01:04.737 --> 00:01:06.671
can use the Reset button to restore

00:01:06.697 --> 00:01:09.789
the original example You can also use

00:01:09.816 --> 00:01:11.237
the Copy button if you want to

00:01:11.263 --> 00:01:13.947
paste the example into Jupyter Notebook Google

00:01:13.974 --> 00:01:17.842
Colab or Visual Studio Code One important

00:01:17.868 --> 00:01:19.776
detail is that the spacebar will not

00:01:19.803 --> 00:01:21.276
move to the next slide while you

00:01:21.303 --> 00:01:23.974
are editing code This means you can

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:27.303
type normally inside the editor The basic

00:01:27.329 --> 00:01:30.632
workflow for this module is simple Read

00:01:30.658 --> 00:01:34.789
the idea Run the code Check the

00:01:34.803 --> 00:01:39.289
output Change something small Then apply the

00:01:39.303 --> 00:01:41.132
same pattern to a new example
